<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- A template: codesign doesn't expand variables. scripts/provisioning.py fills in the team
         and bundle id from the provisioning profile (LIKELY_PROFILE) at sign time and checks every
         value against the profile's own Entitlements; build.sh signs with the result
         (build/…/Likely.entitlements.generated). Builds without a profile are signed without
         entitlements. See docs/BUILDING.md.

         keychain-access-groups needs the profile (its allowed groups are "<team id>.*"): it gives the
         app the data-protection keychain group that holds the data key (KeychainKeyStore,
         EncryptionAvailability). Without it, encryption is off.

         Hardened-runtime exceptions: none needed. No App Sandbox: Likely reads other apps'
         accessibility trees and launches agent CLIs. Accessibility is a TCC grant and needs no
         entitlement (Likely no longer uses Screen Recording). Likely sends no Apple Events, so there's no
         automation entitlement (and agents are denied them). -->
    <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
    <string>$(TeamID).$(BundleID)</string>
    <key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
    <string>$(TeamID)</string>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(TeamID).inc.synth.likely</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
